From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Sanders <dsanders11@ucsbalum.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:25:05 -0700
Subject: test: expect UNABLE_TO_GET_ISSUER_CERT_LOCALLY under BoringSSL

BoringSSL rewrote its certificate chain verification and no longer
reports X509_V_ERR_UNABLE_TO_VERIFY_LEAF_SIGNATURE after the verify
callback suppressed X509_V_ERR_UNABLE_TO_GET_ISSUER_CERT_LOCALLY, which
is what Node.js's callback always does:
https://boringssl-review.googlesource.com/c/boringssl/+/103849

A leaf certificate whose issuer is not in the trust store therefore now
fails with UNABLE_TO_GET_ISSUER_CERT_LOCALLY under BoringSSL, while
OpenSSL still reports UNABLE_TO_VERIFY_LEAF_SIGNATURE. Export the
expected code from test/common/crypto as sslVerificationFailureError and
use it in the affected tests.

Will attempt to upstream this change to Node.js.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

